# This repository tracks configuration files directly in $HOME, so the default
# is to ignore everything and re-include tracked paths explicitly.
#
# Two git rules drive the structure below:
#   1. A file cannot be re-included if one of its parent directories is
#      excluded, so each level must be un-ignored before its contents can be.
#      This is why ~/.config needs three rules rather than one.
#   2. The last matching pattern wins, which is what makes the safety net at
#      the bottom of this file authoritative.
#
# To start tracking something new, add an explicit negation here rather than
# reaching for "git add -f".

/*

# --- Shell and X session ----------------------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/.Xresources
!/.xsessionrc
!/.bashrc
!/.zshrc
!/.fbtermrc

# --- Window manager and session configs -------------------------------------
!/.desktop-session/
!/.fluxbox/
!/.icewm/
!/.jwm/

# Session runtime state, not configuration.
/.desktop-session/*.log
/.desktop-session/old-log-*
/.desktop-session/ppid.*

# --- ~/.config --------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-include the directory, exclude everything inside it, then re-include only
# the subdirectories actually tracked. The /.config/* line is load-bearing:
# without it this section would pull in browser profiles, caches and tokens.
!/.config/
/.config/*
!/.config/i3/
!/.config/i3status/
!/.config/autostart/
!/.config/gtk-3.0/
!/.config/roxterm.sourceforge.net/

# --- Scripts and documentation ----------------------------------------------
!/bin/
!/docs/

# --- ~/.local/bin -----------------------------------------------------------
# Same three-level dance as ~/.config, but tighter: this directory also holds
# uv, the Antigravity CLI and a symlink into the Claude install, which are
# hundreds of megabytes of binaries. Negate individual scripts, never the
# directory.
!/.local/
/.local/*
!/.local/bin/
/.local/bin/*
!/.local/bin/fbt

# --- Display layout ---------------------------------------------------------
# ~/.screenlayout/default.sh sets the panel resolution and is run at every
# session start by autoscale-antix. Losing it means losing the readable
# desktop, so it is tracked rather than left as local-only state.
!/.screenlayout/

# --- Safety net -------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository has a public remote (github.com/rtodea/antix-home). The
# paths below must never be committed regardless of any negation above, so
# they are listed last and therefore win.
.ssh/
.gnupg/
.kube/
.aws/
.docker/
.netrc
.env
*.pem
*.key
*_rsa
*_ed25519
id_*
credentials
